<title>UK: HORSE RACING-INTERNATIONAL STAKES RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-INTERNATIONAL STAKES RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>YORK, England 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group one</p>
<p>International Stakes for three-year-olds and upwards, run over</p>
<p>one and a quarter miles (2 kms) on Tuesday:</p>
<p>1. Singspiel 4-1 (ridden by Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p>2. Desert King 6-1 (Mick Kinane)</p>
<p>3. Benny The Dip 9-2 (Willie Ryan)</p>
<p>Four ran</p>
<p>Bosra Sham (Pat Eddery) 5-4 on favourite</p>
<p>Distances: one and a half lengths, same</p>
<p>Winner owned by Sheikh Mohammed and trained at Newmarket,</p>
<p>England by Michael Stoute.</p>
<p>    Value to winning owner: 202,152 pounds ($324,000)</p>
</text>
